(Bug #70: the `treating` clause belongs to the `each` clause that binds the
 loop variable, not after the append destination. The grammar summary used
 to give it in this position; the sentence is now refused by name, with the
 corrected spelling on the help line.)

a list called names is ["ann", "-"].
a list called out is [].
append each name from names to out treating "-" as "anon".
